{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_24.march","start_line":25,"start_col":2,"end_line":28,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` performs IO but declares no grant. The program reaches `IO.Console`; a `main` with no capability parameter is granted nothing.\nhelp: declare the grant `main` actually needs —\n        fn main(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console)) : ()\nor grant everything with `fn main(cap : Cap(IO))`.\n`forge fix` can apply this.","code":"cap_grant","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":25,"start_col":9,"end_line":25,"end_col":11,"text":"(_cap_console : Cap(IO.Console))"},"labels":[],"notes":[]}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_grant_24.march","start_line":26,"start_col":18,"end_line":26,"end_col":24,"message":"`spawn` needs a plain actor name written directly, like `spawn(Counter)`.\nA computed actor expression (from an `if`, `match`, or function call) isn't supported: March resolves which actor to spawn at compile time from its name.","code":"spawn_computed_actor","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
